From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:04:59 -0700
Subject: [navigation] Match MHTML MIME types case-insensitively in the browser

Per RFC 2045 Section 5.1, media types and subtypes are case-insensitive.
However, browser process MHTML classification in
NavigationRequest::IsMhtmlMimeType(), download_utils::MustDownload(),
and IntentHandler.isMhtmlMimeType() used exact, case-sensitive string
equality for "multipart/related" and "message/rfc822". Meanwhile,
non-HTTP loaders like Android's ContentURLLoader forwarded unnormalized
MIME types from ContentProvider.getType().

Bug: 574381704
Change-Id: I5aa204c725c075d36ee31f7bafebda89b5f4fe58
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8620417
Reviewed-by: Ted Choc <tedchoc@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Nasko Oskov <nasko@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725439}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): content/browser/navigation_mhtml_browsertest.cc is test-only and conflicted; it is not carried.

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/IntentHandler.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/IntentHandler.java
index 6fdac3bc4f88ca05458b68eac353f5c67e550281..2890146ca4d91422d57ba457c9b51d61ee4540cb 100644
--- a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/IntentHandler.java
+++ b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/IntentHandler.java
@@ -1351,7 +1351,8 @@ public class IntentHandler {
 
     /** Return true if the type is one of the Mime types used for MHTML */
     static boolean isMhtmlMimeType(String type) {
-        return type.equals("multipart/related") || type.equals("message/rfc822");
+        return type.equalsIgnoreCase("multipart/related")
+                || type.equalsIgnoreCase("message/rfc822");
     }
 
     /**
